            "text": "In `Core::swap_6269342730()`, when the current `sqrtRatio` equals the `sqrtRatioLimit`, the swap is treated as a no-op, and the entire swap block is skipped. This includes the critical `_updatePairDebtWithNative()` call, which means ETH sent via `msg.value` is never accounted for in the debt system. The ETH becomes permanently stuck in the Core contract with no recovery mechanism."
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "e_be7fd2bc7865_0019",
            "text": "The vulnerability exists in `Core::swap_6269342730()` where the `_updatePairDebtWithNative()` function is placed inside a conditional block that gets skipped when `sqrtRatio == sqrtRatioLimit`."
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "e_be7fd2bc7865_0027",
            "text": "- In `Core::swap_6269342730()`, the condition `stateAfter.sqrtRatio() != sqrtRatioLimit` is FALSE."
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "e_be7fd2bc7865_0028",
            "text": "- The entire swap block (lines 542-843) is skipped, including `_updatePairDebtWithNative()`."
